# Resolve Live Objects Inside run()

`Runnable`, `BukkitRunnable`, and other deferred/scheduled work must not capture live CivCraft or Bukkit objects as fields. Store stable identifiers and resolve through `CivGlobal` (or `Bukkit.getPlayer(UUID)`) at the start of `run()`.

## Why

Town, Civilization, Resident, Player, Buildable, Structure, Farm, and Windmill instances can be removed, replaced, or mutated on other threads between scheduling and execution. A captured reference may be stale or unsafe.

## Forbidden fields in scheduled tasks

- `Town`, `Civilization`, `Resident`
- `Player`, `OfflinePlayer`
- `Buildable`, `Structure`, `Farm`, `Windmill`
- Any holder that embeds them (`FarmZone`, `WindmillReport` with a live `Windmill`, etc.)

## Allowed identifiers

| Type | Store | Resolve in run() |
|------|-------|------------------|
| Town | `int townId` | `CivGlobal.getTownFromId(townId)` |
| Civ | `int civId` or name | `CivGlobal.getCiv(civId)` |
| Resident | `UUID` or `int id` | `CivGlobal.getResident(uuid)` |
| Player | `UUID` | `Bukkit.getPlayer(uuid)` |
| Buildable / Structure / Farm / Windmill | `int buildableId` | `CivGlobal.getBuildable(id)` + instanceof check |

Immutable snapshots taken at schedule time (e.g. `ChunkSnapshot`, `Location`, `CropType`, copied `FarmBlock` slot state) are fine.

## Examples

```java
// ❌ BAD — captures live Farm across async → sync handoff
public class FarmAutoHarvestSync implements Runnable {
    private final Farm farm;

    public FarmAutoHarvestSync(Farm farm, List<FarmBlock> matureBlocks) {
        this.farm = farm;
    }
}

// ✅ GOOD — resolve when the task runs
public class FarmAutoHarvestSync implements Runnable {
    private final int farmId;

    public FarmAutoHarvestSync(int farmId, List<FarmBlock> matureBlocks) {
        this.farmId = farmId;
    }

    @Override
    public void run() {
        Buildable buildable = CivGlobal.getBuildable(this.farmId);
        if (!(buildable instanceof Farm farm) || !farm.isActive()) {
            return;
        }
        // use farm...
    }
}
```

```java
// ❌ BAD — Player reference in delayed task
private final Player player;

// ✅ GOOD
private final UUID playerId;
// run(): Player player = Bukkit.getPlayer(this.playerId);
```

## Constructor parameters

Constructors may accept live objects only to extract IDs and immutable data. Do not assign the live object to a field.

```java
// ✅ GOOD — extract id in constructor, same pattern as HourlyFarmingTask
public HourlyFarmingTask(Town town) {
    this.townId = town.getId();
}
```

Always null-check after lookup; if the entity was removed, return early.
